{"count":1095,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=9&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=7&page_size=100","results":[{"id":906,"title":"On the involvement of former soldiers in Gov Degamo's slay","slug":"on-the-involvement-of-former-soldiers-in-gov-degamos-slay","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The tragic shooting incident that resulted in the death of Gov Degamo in Negros Oriental last Saturday, reportedly involved former soldiers.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-07T16:22:20+08:00","hits":242},{"id":907,"title":"AFP Statement on the Death of Negros Oriental Governor","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-death-of-negros-oriental-governor","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div>The Armed Forces of the Philippines condemns the brutal act committed by the assailants that caused the death of Negros Oriental Governor Roel Degamo and eight other civilians and the wounding of 16 others, including two of our soldiers.</div>\r\n<div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-05T16:18:19+08:00","hits":171},{"id":908,"title":"123 Terrorists Neutralized, 136 Firearms gained by AFP in February","slug":"123-terrorists-neutralized-136-firearms-gained-by-afp-in-february","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/IMG-ea4363e5deda7f013d9fd24d384226a8-V.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/IMG-ea4363e5deda7f013d9fd24d384226a8-V.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) has registered for February a total of 123 neutralized terrorists along with 136 firearms gained in various focused military and support to law enforcement operations across the country.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> ","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/IMG-ea4363e5deda7f013d9fd24d384226a8-V.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-05T09:57:24+08:00","hits":214},{"id":909,"title":"7 NPA terrorists yield to AFP in Davao Del Norte","slug":"7-npa-terrorists-yield-to-afp-in-davao-del-norte","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 7 NPA terrorists yield to AFP in Davao Del Norte.jpg\" width=\"854\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04122022 7 NPA terrorists yield to AFP in Davao Del Norte.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Seven communist NPA terrorists (CNTs) yielded to the 56th Infantry Battalion of the 1003rd Infantry Brigade under the Philippine Army's 10th Infantry Division (10ID) in Talaingod, Davao del Norte, on April 8.</p>\r\n<p>Lieutenant Colonel Osmalik Tayaban identified the surrenderees on their aliases as Mamiloy, Onyok, Trisha, Toryo/Dayan, Mars, Marvin, Dante (true names withheld for their protection). They brought two (2) AK47 Rifles and one (1) IMI Israel AR Galil Rifle.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04122022%207%20NPA%20terrorists%20yield%20to%20AFP%20in%20Davao%20Del%20Norte.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-04T10:54:49+08:00","hits":454},{"id":910,"title":"“Don’t quit,” says AFP Chief of Staff to PMA “Talang Dangal” Class 2026","slug":"don-t-quit-says-afp-chief-of-staff-to-pma-talang-dangal-class-2026","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/IMG-a07ba8ab3979472197a3c6f93ac51d28-V.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"535\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/IMG-a07ba8ab3979472197a3c6f93ac51d28-V.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres C Centino PA, served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the Recognition Rites of the Philippine Military Academy “Talang Dangal” Class of 2026 on Saturday, March 04, 2023, at Fort Del Pilar, Baguio City.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The CSAFP, who belongs to PMA “Maringal” Class of 1988, was welcomed by the Officers, Enlisted Personnel, Cadets, and Civilian Human Resources at the Academy under the leadership of PMA Superintendent LtGen Rowen S Tolentino PA.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">In his remarks, the CSAFP addressed four audiences: the fourthclass cadets or plebes; the upperclass cadets; the families and loved ones of the plebes; and the entire PMA. As an alumnus of the Academy, he shared the same pride as a cadet 39 years ago and asked the 310 newly-recognized cadets to “manifest the level of maturity and sense of responsibility worthy of the trust and respect of your upperclassmen and mentors.”</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">“In the days ahead, we will ask even more of you, in the fortitude of spirit, keenness of mind, and generosity of camaraderie. But know that the more challenging the times become, the better prepared you will be for the demands and trials that await you once you are outside of the Academy,” as the CSAFP shared one of the most important plebe-knowledges that he kept to his heart, the poem “Don’t Quit.”</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> ","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/IMG-a07ba8ab3979472197a3c6f93ac51d28-V.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-04T01:51:43+08:00","hits":643},{"id":911,"title":"AFP welcomes new Sergeant Major","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-sergeant-major","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Armed Forces of the Philippines conducted a Change of Chief of Office and Retirement Ceremony for the AFP Sergeant Major (AFPSM) with the Chief of Staff, AFP, General Andres C Centino PA as the Presiding Officer on March 03, 2023 at the AFP General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Change of Chief of Office Ceremony also marked the retirement of the outgoing AFPSM, First Chief Master Sergeant Rogelio O Obillo PN(M). He turned over his duties to the incoming AFPSM, Master Chief Petty Officer Joe Marie V Lucero PN, who took the post in an acting capacity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-03T09:51:36+08:00","hits":1169},{"id":912,"title":"Be a hero to our heroes' children in the 6th HERO Golf Cup","slug":"be-a-hero-to-our-heroes-children-in-the-6th-hero-golf-cup-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/HR1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"1146\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/HR1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The HERO Golf Cup is an annual charity golf tournament organized by the HERO (Help Educate and Rear Orphans) Foundation, Inc. Now on its 6th year, all proceeds of the tournament will go to help fund the educational needs of orphaned children and dependent siblings of soldiers who were permanently incapacitated or killed due to enemy action or during disaster relief operations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/HR1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-03T09:49:54+08:00","hits":270},{"id":913,"title":"AFP Vice Chief talks to troops, advocates Gender and Development","slug":"afp-vice-chief-talks-to-troops-advocates-gender-and-development","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/G4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"507\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/G4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Vice Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (VCSAFP), LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF, conducted a talk to the troops advocating Gender and Development at the AFP General Headquarters today, March 02, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BGen Armand M Arevalo PA, commander of the General Headquarters and Headquarters Service Command, AFP (GHQ &amp; HSC, AFP) welcomed LtGen Cordura, who is also the Chairperson of the AFP Gender and Development Focal Point System Executive Committee.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/G4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-02T09:46:21+08:00","hits":488},{"id":914,"title":"Four NPA terrorists killed, six firearms seized in Negros Occidental encounter","slug":"four-npa-terrorists-killed-six-firearms-seized-in-negros-occidental-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/viber_image_2023-03-02_10-50-14-176.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"603\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/viber_image_2023-03-02_10-50-14-176.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Four members of the communist terrorist group (CTG) were killed in an encounter with troops of the 94th Infantry Battalion in Himamaylan City, Negros Occidental on March 1.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Responding to information from residents, the soldiers conducted combat operations against the communist terrorists who were extorting food and supplies in Barangay Carabalan. This resulted in the encounter against around 20 CTG members, yielding six firearms consisting of 2 M16 rifles, 2 M203 grenade launchers, and 2 AK47 rifles.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/viber_image_2023-03-02_10-50-14-176.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-02T09:43:52+08:00","hits":197},{"id":915,"title":"AFP Educational Benefit System Office holds Golf-for-a-Cause for more than 2,000 military orphans","slug":"afp-educational-benefit-system-office-holds-golf-for-a-cause-for-more-than-2-000-military-orphans","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/viber_image_2023-03-01_16-52-22-112.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/viber_image_2023-03-01_16-52-22-112.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines through its Educational Benefit System Office (AFPEBSO) conducted a golf-for-a-cause tournament dedicated to the dependents of Killed-in-Action (KIA) military personnel on March 01, 2023, at the Camp Aguinaldo Golf Club, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The activity, dubbed “F.O.R.E.: Fund for the Orphans’ Registration and Education,” aims to support the education of the grantees who are dependents of soldiers who sacrificed their lives protecting the peace in the country.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-01T09:41:38+08:00","hits":411},{"id":916,"title":"Philippine Inter-Agency Contingent returns from Turkiye mission","slug":"philippine-inter-agency-contingent-returns-from-turkiye-mission","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/viber_image_2023-03-01_09-28-34-350.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"531\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/viber_image_2023-03-01_09-28-34-350.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP joined other government agency officials in welcoming the Philippine Inter-Agency Humanitarian Contingent (PIAHC) to Turkiye on February 28 at the Ninoy Aquino International Airport.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The PIAHC was deployed in Turkiye on February 8 to conduct humanitarian assistance and disaster response operations following the magnitude 7.8 earthquake that hit the country.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/viber_image_2023-03-01_09-28-34-350.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-03-01T09:39:46+08:00","hits":220},{"id":917,"title":"MORALE AND WELFARE","slug":"morale-and-welfare","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE17.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE17.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, visits the troops stationed in Sultan Kudarat, Marawi City, and Cagayan De Oro City today in a campaign to boost the morale and check on the welfare of military personnel on the frontlines.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">In his talk with the troops, he reminded the officers of the importance of seeing firsthand the condition on the ground and being visible to the men and women tasked with maintaining peace and security in far-flung communities.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE17.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:41:36+08:00","hits":843},{"id":918,"title":"AFP reiterates support for international peacekeeping","slug":"afp-reiterates-support-for-international-peacekeeping","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE16.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE16.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP reiterated its support to international peacekeeping as it welcomed LtGen Andrew Harrison, the deputy commander of the UN Command in Korea (UNC-ROK), at the AFP General Headquarters today.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">LtGen William N Gonzales PA, The Inspector General, AFP, welcomed LtGen Harrison and relayed the CSAFP's message of the AFP's steadfast commitment to the UNC-ROK in its mission of keeping the peace in the Korean peninsula.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE16.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:39:10+08:00","hits":308},{"id":920,"title":"TALK TO TROOPS","slug":"talk-to-troops-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE15.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE15.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino PA encourages the troops to maintain discipline and focus on defeating communist NPA terrorists (CNT) during his talk to the troops at Headquarters 6th Infantry Division at Camp Siongco, Awang, Datu Odin Sinsuat, and 601st Infantry Brigade at Barangay Kamasi Ampatuan in Maguindanao on February 23.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE15.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:36:11+08:00","hits":3985},{"id":919,"title":"TALK TO TROOPS","slug":"talk-to-troops","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE15.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE15.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino PA encourages the troops to maintain discipline and focus on defeating communist NPA terrorists (CNT) during his talk to the troops at Headquarters 6th Infantry Division at Camp Siongco, Awang, Datu Odin Sinsuat, and 601st Infantry Brigade at Barangay Kamasi Ampatuan in Maguindanao on February 23.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE15.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:36:11+08:00","hits":4236},{"id":921,"title":"Aus Defense Minister, CSAFP visit Army Troops in 6ID","slug":"aus-defense-minister-csafp-visit-army-troops-in-6id","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE14.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE14.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Andres Centino PA joined Hon. Richard Marles, the Deputy Prime Minister (DPM) and Minister for Defence (MinDef) of Australia on an official visit to the Headquarters, 6th Infantry Division (6ID) of the Philippine Army at Camp Siongco, Awang, Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao today.<br /><br />The Commander of the Western Mindanao Command (WESMINCOM), LtGen Roy Galido PA, along with the 6ID Commander, MGen Alex Rillera PA welcomed Hon. Marles and the CSAFP at the 6ID grounds.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE14.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:34:34+08:00","hits":207},{"id":922,"title":"CSAFP meets with US Naval Operations Chief","slug":"csafp-meets-with-us-naval-operations-chief","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE13.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE13.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-- The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, met with Admiral Michael Gilday, Chief of US Naval Operations, during the latter's courtesy visit today at the AFP General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">After the arrival honors rendered by the AFP, the two proceeded to the meeting that affirmed a robust military partnership between the US and the Philippines based on the Mutual Defense Treaty, including pursuing a free and open Indo-Pacific region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE13.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:32:04+08:00","hits":234},{"id":923,"title":"AFP welcomes new operations chief","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-operations-chief","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE12.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"711\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE12.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP installed BGen Fernando M Reyeg as its new Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations, J3, in a Change of Chief of Office Ceremony presided by The Deputy Chief of Staff, VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes today at the AFP General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A member of the PMA Sambisig Class of 1991, BGen Reyeg comes in from his stint as the Assistant Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training, and Doctrine, AJ8. Prior to this, he served in various command and staff positions, including as the commander of the erstwhile 104th Infantry Brigade (now 101st Infantry Brigade) and at the same time Joint Task Force Basilan; commander of the 3rd Scout Ranger Battalion; Chief of Readiness and Organization Division and Plans, Policy, and Programs Division of OJ3; and Chief of Staff of 6th Infantry Division and Chief the of Unified Command Staff of Western Mindanao Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE12.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:30:24+08:00","hits":1857},{"id":924,"title":"AFP Statement on WPD","slug":"afp-statement-on-wpd","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Primordial in every action taken by the Armed Forces of the Philippines is its constitutional duty to protect the people and the state. It shall always be true and committed to its mission of safeguarding our country’s sovereignty and territorial integrity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:28:52+08:00","hits":240},{"id":925,"title":"PMA ALUMNI HOMECOMING","slug":"pma-alumni-homecoming","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>The Chief of Staff, AFP and other graduates of the institution join the Philippine Military Academy Alumni Homecoming honored with the presence of the Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr today.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE11.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:26:39+08:00","hits":252},{"id":926,"title":"Introduction to Operational Planning Course","slug":"introduction-to-operational-planning-course","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE10.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE10.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The five-day Introduction to Operational Planning Course (IOPC) sponsored by the Canadian Directorate of Military Training and Cooperation and co-hosted by the AFP concludes with a closing ceremony held at Widus Hotel, Clark, Pampanga today, February 17, 2023.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE10.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:24:53+08:00","hits":155},{"id":927,"title":"AFP Statement on the death of 2Lt Nico Malcampo","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-death-of-2lt-nico-malcampo","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP extends its sincerest condolences to the family of 2Lt Nico Malcampo of the 9th Infantry Division, Philippine Army. His sacrifice will not be in vain as we push forward in our mission to bring to justice every communist terrorist and fully end the communist armed conflict in the country.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:22:40+08:00","hits":228},{"id":928,"title":"\"Our fellow Filipinos deserve better\", CSAFP reminds troops in his visit to Southern Luzon Command","slug":"our-fellow-filipinos-deserve-better-csafp-reminds-troops-in-his-visit-to-southern-luzon-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE9.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE9.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), Gen Andres C Centino PA visited today the headquarters of Southern Luzon Command (SOLCOM) in Lucena City. He was welcomed by SOLCOM Commander LtGen Efren Baluyot PA.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his talk to the troops, the CSAFP personally conveyed the AFP's thrusts of operational efficiency, optimal use of resources, advancing professionalism and meritocracy, and capability development.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE9.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:20:06+08:00","hits":242},{"id":929,"title":"AFP Statement on the Call of Ambassador of China in the Philippines to the CSAFP","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-call-of-ambassador-of-china-in-the-philippines-to-the-csafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>His Excellency Huang Xilian, the Ambassador of China in the Philippines, paid his courtesy call to the Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Andres C Centino PA, yesterday afternoon an activity that has long been scheduled.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:17:29+08:00","hits":197},{"id":930,"title":"Army's 85IB facilitates surrender of NPAs and supporters; discovers arms cache in Quezon Province","slug":"armys-85ib-facilitates-surrender-of-npas-and-supporters-discovers-arms-cache-in-quezon-province","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE8.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE8.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Philippine Army's 85th Infantry Battalion (85IB) facilitated the surrender of 6 communist NPA terrorists (CNT) and 75 supporters in Quezon Province since February 13.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Two CNT members and 21 supporters abandoned their group in San Andres, Quezon on February 14 when they surrendered to 85IB, PNP, and LGU of San Andres.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE8.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:15:02+08:00","hits":325},{"id":931,"title":"CSAFP honors fallen marines on a visit to Marine Corps headquarters","slug":"csafp-honors-fallen-marines-on-a-visit-to-marine-corps-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, honored fallen officers and enlisted personnel of the Philippine Marine Corps (PMC) as he led the wreath-laying ceremony at the Marine Heroes Memorial at their headquarters in Taguig City, today.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">He was assisted by PMC Commandant MGen. Charlton Sean M. Gaerlan, who also welcomed the CSAFP together with his staff.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE7.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:12:15+08:00","hits":175},{"id":932,"title":"AFP welcomes new Chief ISAFP; DCS for Intelligence, J2","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-chief-isafp-dcs-for-intelligence-j2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/RE6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony for the Deputy Chief of Staff (DCS) for Intelligence, J2, and the Assumption of Command Ceremony of the Chief, Intelligence Service, AFP (ISAFP) on 13 February.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ceremonies were presided over by The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes PN.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/RE6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:10:07+08:00","hits":9907},{"id":933,"title":"AFP, DND join DOTr and SMMC in Metro Manila Subway Project Groundbreaking Ceremony","slug":"afp-dnd-join-dotr-and-smmc-in-metro-manila-subway-project-groundbreaking-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/RE5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/RE5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Department of National Defense (DND) joined the Department of Transportation (DOTr) and the Sumitomo Mitsui Construction Co., Ltd. (SMMC) in the Groundbreaking Ceremony of the Metro Manila Subway Project (MMSP) at Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo today, February 13.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Quezon City Mayor Ma. Josefina Belmonte welcomed the attendees during the ceremony, including the Chief of Staff, AFP, General Andres Centino PA; OIC, DND UnderSecretary Carlito Galvez, Jr.; Transportation Secretary Jaime Bautista; Quezon City 3rd District Representative Franz Pumaren; SMCC Project Director Hitoshi Yamaji; JICA Chief Representative Sakamoto Takema; and other officials from the Embassy of Japan.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/RE5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:07:33+08:00","hits":374},{"id":934,"title":"AFP co-hosts a military training course with the Canadian Armed Forces","slug":"afp-co-hosts-a-military-training-course-with-the-canadian-armed-forces","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/RE4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/RE4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines co-hosts a 5-day military operational planning course with the Canadian Armed Forces starting today in Clark, Pampanga.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Thirty-five officers from the AFP and the armed forces of Bangladesh, Indonesia, Mongolia, Malaysia, Nepal, Thailand, and Vietnam are attending the course.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/RE4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T16:04:27+08:00","hits":215},{"id":935,"title":"CSAFP visits Philippine Navy, reiterates thrusts","slug":"csafp-visits-philippine-navy-reiterates-thrusts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/RE3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/RE3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, visited the Philippine Navy Headquarters in Manila today. He was welcomed by officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resources of the Philippine Navy led by the Flag Officer In Command, VAdm Toribio D Adaci Jr.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his talk to troops, the CSAFP reminded every sailor and marine of his thrusts of operational efficiency, optimal use of resources, professionalism and meritocracy, and capability development.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/RE3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T15:58:08+08:00","hits":208},{"id":936,"title":"AFP sends urban search and rescue teams as part of Philippine delegation to Turkey","slug":"afp-sends-urban-search-and-rescue-teams-as-part-of-philippine-delegation-to-turkey","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/RE2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/RE2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The AFP sends its urban search and rescue (USAR) teams from the Philippine Army's 525th Engineer Combat Battalion, 51st Engineer Brigade and the Philippine Air Force 505th Search and Rescue Group as part of the Philippine delegation to Turkey.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The 33 personnel from the AFP will join USAR units of the MMDA and Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority. In addition, the Office of Civil Defense will send a communications and logistics team, while the Department of Health will dispatch emergency medical personnel to aid the response team of earthquake-stricken Turkey.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/RE2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T15:25:59+08:00","hits":335},{"id":937,"title":"MILITARY TRADITION","slug":"military-tradition","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/RE1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"499\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/RE1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">After taking their oath yesterday before the President, the 77 newly-promoted AFP Generals and Flag Officers led by the Vice Chief of Staff, AFP Lt. Gen. Arthur M Cordura PAF were accorded with traditional Arrival Honors at the General Headquarters on 07 Feb . After that, the new promotees rendered Courtesy Call to the Chief of Staff AFP (CSAFP) Gen. Andres C Centino PA.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/RE1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T15:20:59+08:00","hits":338},{"id":938,"title":"AFP kicks off Dental Health Fair 2023","slug":"afp-kicks-off-dental-health-fair-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/DE8.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/DE8.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines Dental Service kicked off the Dental Health Fair 2023 on February 28, 2023, at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand, Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff, AFP General Andres C Centino PA led the Ribbon Cutting to officially open the Dental Health Fair 2023. He was accompanied by The Chief Dental Service, AFP, BGen Angelica DL Torres DS; Assistant Secretary for Consumer Affairs &amp; Department of Agriculture Spokesperson, Khristine Y Evangelista; Department of Health Representative, Dr. Rochelle E Pambid; and Mrs. Sheila S. Centino.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/DE8.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T09:37:34+08:00","hits":209},{"id":939,"title":"President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr talks with the troops of the Visayas Command","slug":"president-ferdinand-r-marcos-jr-talks-with-the-troops-of-the-visayas-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/FqA9iKAaYAAWdv1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/FqA9iKAaYAAWdv1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Commander-in- Chief, Pres Ferdinand R Marcos Jr talks with the troops of the Visayas Command (VisCom) at BGen Ebuen Air Base, Lapu-Lapu City, Cebu today.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/FqA9iKAaYAAWdv1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T09:34:55+08:00","hits":249},{"id":940,"title":"AFP, DOH break ground on new 2-Storey Ambulatory Care Unit Building","slug":"afp-doh-break-ground-on-new-2-storey-ambulatory-care-unit-building","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/Z1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/Z1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines, through its Health Service Command (AFPHSC), conducted a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a two (2)-storey Ambulatory Care Unit Building today, February 28 at the AFPHSC, Camp Victoriano K. Luna, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p>Present during the event was DOH Assistant Secretary Dr. Leonita P. Gorgolon, representing Undersecretary Dr. Lilibeth C. David, and the AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres C Centino PA.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/Z1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T09:32:53+08:00","hits":180},{"id":941,"title":"UNIT VISIT","slug":"unit-visit","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feb2023/UN7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"535\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feb2023/UN7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Chief of Staff, AFP General Andres C Centino meets the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resources based in Cebu during his visit to the headquarters of the Naval Forces Central (NAVFORCEN) on February 27.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-28T08:41:42+08:00","hits":272},{"id":942,"title":"CSAFP visits troops in Sarangani","slug":"csafp-visits-troops-in-sarangani","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">MORALE AND WELFARE | General Andres C Centino, the CSAFP, meets with the officers and enlisted personnel of the 1002nd Infantry Brigade at Camp Hermenigildo A Agaab Jr, Sitio Pulatana, Brgy Malandag, Malungon Sarangani today as part of his continuing visits to frontline units.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The visit was aimed at personally checking the condition of soldiers on the ground and used the occasion to deliver his guidelines--operational efficiency, optimal use of resources, professionalism and meritocracy, and capability development--and congratulated the unit for its successful campaign against threat groups in their area of responsibility. (Photos by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-26T15:19:02+08:00","hits":3939},{"id":943,"title":"GENDER AND DEVELOPMENT","slug":"gender-and-development","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/59C3FD27-47B8-4AD5-AB9B-FACB8805533C.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/59C3FD27-47B8-4AD5-AB9B-FACB8805533C.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP and Chairperson of the Gender and Development Focal Point System Executive Committee , LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF,</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/59C3FD27-47B8-4AD5-AB9B-FACB8805533C.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-24T15:17:35+08:00","hits":453},{"id":944,"title":"AUS-PHIL ARMY EXERCISE","slug":"aus-phil-army-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/A3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/A3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Andres Centino PA and Hon. Richard Marles, the Deputy Prime Minister (DPM) and Minister for Defence (MinDef) of Australia jointly witness the demonstration of Phil-Australian Army to Amy Counter Terrorism Exercise being conducted at Headquarters 6ID, Camp Siongco, Awang, Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao today.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/A3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-23T15:14:02+08:00","hits":197},{"id":945,"title":"\"Our fellow Filipinos deserve better\", CSAFP reminds troops in his visit to Southern Luzon Command","slug":"our-fellow-filipinos-deserve-better-csafp-reminds-troops-in-his-visit-to-southern-luzon-command-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2023/Our fellow Filipinos deserve better CSAFP reminds troops in his visit to Southern Luzon Command.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2023/Our fellow Filipinos deserve better CSAFP reminds troops in his visit to Southern Luzon Command.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), Gen Andres C Centino PA visited today the headquarters of Southern Luzon Command (SOLCOM) in Lucena City. He was welcomed by SOLCOM Commander LtGen Efren Baluyot PA.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202023/Our%20fellow%20Filipinos%20deserve%20better%20CSAFP%20reminds%20troops%20in%20his%20visit%20to%20Southern%20Luzon%20Command.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-17T03:07:05+08:00","hits":122},{"id":946,"title":"Army's 85IB facilitates surrender of NPAs and supporters; discovers arms cache in Quezon Province","slug":"armys-85ib-facilitates-surrender-of-npas-and-supporters-discovers-arms-cache-in-quezon-province-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2023/Armys 85IB facilitates surrender of NPAs and supporters discovers arms cache in Quezon Province.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2023/Armys 85IB facilitates surrender of NPAs and supporters discovers arms cache in Quezon Province.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Philippine Army's 85th Infantry Battalion (85IB) facilitated the surrender of 6 communist NPA terrorists (CNT) and 75 supporters in Quezon Province since February 13.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202023/Armys%2085IB%20facilitates%20surrender%20of%20NPAs%20and%20supporters%20discovers%20arms%20cache%20in%20Quezon%20Province.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-17T03:03:22+08:00","hits":132},{"id":947,"title":"CSAFP honors fallen marines on a visit to Marine Corps headquarters","slug":"csafp-honors-fallen-marines-on-a-visit-to-marine-corps-headquarters-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2023/CSAFP honors fallen marines on a visit to Marine Corps headquarters.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2023/CSAFP honors fallen marines on a visit to Marine Corps headquarters.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, honored fallen officers and enlisted personnel of the Philippine Marine Corps (PMC) as he led the wreath-laying ceremony at the Marine Heroes Memorial at their headquarters in Taguig City, today.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202023/CSAFP%20honors%20fallen%20marines%20on%20a%20visit%20to%20Marine%20Corps%20headquarters.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-17T02:59:19+08:00","hits":118},{"id":948,"title":"AFP receives 'excellent' satisfaction rating in the latest SWS Survey","slug":"afp-receives-excellent-satisfaction-rating","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb 2023/AFP receives excellent satisfaction rating in the latest SWS Survey.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Feb 2023/AFP receives excellent satisfaction rating in the latest SWS Survey.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received a high public satisfaction rating for its performance, with an \"excellent +76\" net score, according to the recent December 2022 Social Weather Stations (SWS) Survey.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Feb%202023/AFP%20receives%20excellent%20satisfaction%20rating%20in%20the%20latest%20SWS%20Survey.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-17T02:52:21+08:00","hits":122},{"id":949,"title":"AFP Related Links","slug":"afp-related-links","category":4,"category_name":"AFP LOGOS","category_slug":"afp-logos","intro_html":"<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: Auto;\" border=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 204.797px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.7627%; height: 204.797px;\"><a title=\"dnd\" href=\"https://www.dnd.gov.ph/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/afp related logos/dnd.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/afp related logos/dnd.png\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.7627%; text-align: center; height: 204.797px;\"><a title=\"pharmy\" href=\"https://army.mil.ph/home/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/afp related logos/army.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/afp related logos/army.png\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.7627%; height: 204.797px;\"><a title=\"pn\" href=\"https://navy.mil.ph/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/afp related logos/navy.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/afp related logos/navy.png\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.7627%; height: 204.797px;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/afp related logos/paf.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/afp related logos/paf.png\" /></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.7639%; height: 204.797px;\"><a title=\"pma\" href=\"https://www.pma.edu.ph/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/afp related logos/PMA Seal.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/afp related logos/PMA Seal.png\" /></a></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-16T12:36:51+08:00","hits":5},{"id":950,"title":"Oathtaking of AFP generals and flag officers in Malacañan Palace","slug":"oathtaking-of-afp-generals-and-flag-officers-in-malacanan-palace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/oath1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/oath1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP is grateful to our President and Commander-in-Chief for personally officiating the oathtaking of the newly-promoted AFP Generals and Flag Officers on 06 February, at the Malacañan Palace.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/oath1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-07T15:11:49+08:00","hits":272},{"id":951,"title":"Transparency Seal","slug":"transparency-seal","category":3,"category_name":"Transparency Seal and FOI","category_slug":"transparency-seal-and-foi","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/rel-links/trans.jpg\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/rel-links/trans.jpg\" /></p>","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-07T00:41:06+08:00","hits":83},{"id":952,"title":"AFP Statement on EDCA and Balikatan Exercises","slug":"afp-statement-on-edca-and-balikatan-exercises","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines expresses its gratitude for the support extended by Senators Francis Tolentino, Francis Escudero and Sherwin Gatchalian to the implementation of the Enhanced Defense Cooperation Agreement (EDCA). This manifestation of support is in line with our treaty obligation as contained in the Mutual Defense Treaty of 1951.<br /><br />Since the signing of EDCA in 2014, it has continuously facilitated the conduct of military exercises and HADR operations in support to the AFP mission. Likewise, with the threat of climate change, our partnership with modern and well-equipped countries such as the United States of America will develop the capability of our troops in executing humanitarian and disaster response (HADR) operations in times of natural calamities and disasters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-06T15:08:51+08:00","hits":312},{"id":953,"title":"PH-US MILITARY RELATIONS","slug":"ph-us-military-relations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">AFP Vice Chief of Staff, LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF welcomed LtGen George W Smith Jr during his courtesy visit on February 3 at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. LtGen Smith Jr, commanding general of the US I Marine Expeditionary Force, is in the country in preparation for Balikatan Exercise in April 2023.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-06T15:05:31+08:00","hits":581},{"id":954,"title":"AFP Statement","slug":"afp-statement","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Enhanced Defense Cooperation Agreement (EDCA) is a collaborative agreement between the United States and the Philippines that enables both countries to increase joint training opportunities, humanitarian assistance and disaster response (HADR) capability, and rotational activities to strengthen interoperability between our armed forces.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-06T15:03:54+08:00","hits":400},{"id":956,"title":"Donning of Ranks","slug":"donning-of-ranks-3","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/viber_image_2023-02-03_15-55-19-522.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, donned new ranks to Commander of Western Mindanao Command (WMC), LtGen Roy M Galido PA, and two other senior officers on Friday, February 3 at the General Headquarters, Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo, Quezon City.<br /><br />Joining the WCM Commander were Commodore Marcos Y Imperio PN, the Commander of the Communication, Electronics, and Information Systems Service AFP (CEISSAFP); and, reservist BGen Eric C Garchitorena MC, Commander of the 1st Technical and Administrative Services (TAS) Brigade - NCR Reserve Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/viber_image_2023-02-03_15-55-19-522.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-03T14:59:19+08:00","hits":527},{"id":955,"title":"Donning of Ranks","slug":"donning-of-ranks-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/viber_image_2023-02-03_15-55-19-522.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, donned new ranks to Commander of Western Mindanao Command (WMC), LtGen Roy M Galido PA, and two other senior officers on Friday, February 3 at the General Headquarters, Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo, Quezon City.<br /><br />Joining the WCM Commander were Commodore Marcos Y Imperio PN, the Commander of the Communication, Electronics, and Information Systems Service AFP (CEISSAFP); and, reservist BGen Eric C Garchitorena MC, Commander of the 1st Technical and Administrative Services (TAS) Brigade - NCR Reserve Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/viber_image_2023-02-03_15-55-19-522.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-03T14:59:19+08:00","hits":263},{"id":957,"title":"3 local terrorists surrender in Maguindanao Del Sur","slug":"3-local-terrorists-surrender-in-maguindanao-del-sur","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/viber_image_2023-02-03_12-28-31-353.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"513\" /></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> – Three (3) members of the Bangsamoro Islamic Freedom Fighters-Karialan Faction (BIFF-KF) and Bungos Faction (BF) voluntarily surrendered to the 40th Infantry Battalion (H40IB) in Brgy. Kabengi, Datu Saudi, Ampatuan, Maguindanao Del Sur on February 01, 2023.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/viber_image_2023-02-03_12-28-31-353.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-03T14:50:23+08:00","hits":181},{"id":958,"title":"PH-US DEFENSE RELATIONS ","slug":"ph-us-defense-relations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres C Centino PA, joined Secretary of National Defense Carlito G Galvez Jr in welcoming US Secretary of Defense Lloyd J Austin III during his visit to the Department of National Defense on February 2, 2023.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-02T14:47:18+08:00","hits":169},{"id":959,"title":"CTG IN VISAYAS CONTINUES TO CRUMBLE, AFP SUSTAINS THE MOMENTUM","slug":"ctg-in-visayas-continues-to-crumble-afp-sustains-the-momentum","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"526\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Camp Lapulapu, Cebu City – The Communist Terrorist Group (CTG) in the Visayas region continues to crumble as the AFP under the Visayas Command (VISCOM) sustains its momentum.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We have achieved significant gains in our efforts and will continue to push on. There will be no let-up in our Focused Military Operation and Community Support Program as we sustain the momentum and prevent the CTG from ever gaining their footing in the region,” said Lieutenant General Benedict M Arevalo PA, the Commander of VISCOM.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-02-01T14:43:25+08:00","hits":309},{"id":960,"title":"LGU hands over 23 loose firearms in Basilan","slug":"lgu-hands-over-23-loose-firearms-in-basilan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/A2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The JTF Basilan along with Basilan police and chief executives received 23 loose firearms turned over by Hadji Muhtamad Mayor Arsina Nanoh on January 30 as part of the government's efforts to curb the proliferation of illegal weapons in the region.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/A2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-31T14:40:31+08:00","hits":249},{"id":961,"title":"CSAFP to Armor Div troops: Attitude, values, essential to be world-class","slug":"csafp-to-armor-div-troops-attitude-values-essential-to-be-world-class","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/ARM8.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Andres Centino PA, Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), addressed the Armor (Pambato) Division, Philippine Army, during his visit to Camp O'Donnell, Sta. Lucia, Capas, Tarlac on January 30, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his talk to the \"mounted warriors,\" CSAFP spoke of the AFP's accomplishments in combating several threats and problems in the country. However, he emphasized that though the insurgency threat has been significantly reduced, more efforts are needed to pave the way for an environment conducive to progress and development.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/ARM8.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-30T14:36:38+08:00","hits":330},{"id":962,"title":"DONNING OF RANKS","slug":"donning-of-ranks","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/11.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes PN, presided over the donning of ranks ceremony on January 30 for the newly promoted officers of the Philippine Navy assigned at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/11.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-30T14:34:02+08:00","hits":1435},{"id":963,"title":"AFP welcomes new Internal Auditor, Logistics Chief relinquishes post","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-internal-auditor-logistics-chief-relinquishes-post","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/a.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a Change of Chief of Office Ceremony welcoming the new The Internal Auditor (TIA) in Camp Aguinaldo on January 27, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ceremony, which installed Brigadier General Joel Alejandro S Nacnac as the new TIA, was presided over by Lieutenant General Arthur M Cordura PAF, Vice Chief of Staff, AFP.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/a.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-27T14:29:15+08:00","hits":1080},{"id":964,"title":"AFP Statement on the SF-260 mishap","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-sf-260-mishap","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\r\n<p>The AFP extends its sincerest condolences to the families and friends of the two Philippine Air Force pilots who perished in the SF-260 air mishap in Bataan on January 25.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-26T14:25:43+08:00","hits":226},{"id":965,"title":"LtGen Torres retires from service, relinquishes post as NOLCOM commander","slug":"ltgen-torres-retires-from-service-relinquishes-post-as-nolcom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/327423037_2111566892368242_2581252322198253873_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--LtGen Ernesto C Torres PA relinquished his post as commander of NOLCOM to MGen Fernyl G Buca PAF in a Joint Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony presided over by the CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, on January 25 in the NOLCOM headquarters in Tarlac.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">LtGen Torres retired from the military after more than 38 years of service as a cadet and officer.His career was highlighted by his appointment to various command positions, including commander of the Civil Relations Service, Joint Task Force Haribon, and 1003rd Infantry Brigade.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/327423037_2111566892368242_2581252322198253873_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-26T14:23:20+08:00","hits":434},{"id":966,"title":"AFP welcomes the new SOCOM commander","slug":"afp-welcomes-the-new-socom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/IMG_8470.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP installed MGen Arturo G Rojas PN(M) as the new commander of the Special Operations Command (SOCOM) in a Change of Command ceremony presided over by the CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA today, January 25 in Fort Magsaysay, Nueva Ecija.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">MGen Rojas takes over SOCOM from its deputy commander, Col Ranulfo A. Sevilla PA, who has been serving in an acting capacity after serving as the Deputy Commander of Western Mindanao Command.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/IMG_8470.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-25T14:19:29+08:00","hits":718},{"id":967,"title":"AFP dons rank to newly promoted generals","slug":"afp-dons-rank-to-newly-promoted-generals","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/IMG_8465.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"713\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The AFP donned ranks to the newly promoted generals in a ceremony presided over by CSAFP General Andres C Centino on January 23 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LtGen Stephen P Parreño PAF, the Air Force Commanding General led the newly promotees along with LtGen Benedict M Arevalo PA, commander of the Visayas Command, and BGen Leodigario V Macalintal, deputy The Inspector General, AFP.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/IMG_8465.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-24T11:05:29+08:00","hits":274},{"id":968,"title":"Senior AFP officers take new posts","slug":"senior-afp-officers-take-new-posts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/BA33FC81-C11B-422A-8169-9F633A88E79E.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"494\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Senior military officers assumed their new posts on Monday, January 23, in a joint Change of Chief of Office Ceremony presided by The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes at the Tejeros Hall here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">MGen Alex S Rillera PA relinquished his post as the Deputy Chief of Staff (DCS) for Operations, J3, to his assistant, BGen Glenn Jun C Calambuhay PA, who will perform the role in an acting capacity. MGen Rillera will later assume as the new commander of the 6th Infantry Division.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/BA33FC81-C11B-422A-8169-9F633A88E79E.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-24T11:01:47+08:00","hits":715},{"id":969,"title":"AFP receives 'excellent' satisfaction rating in the latest SWS Survey","slug":"afp-receives-excellent-satisfaction-rating-in-the-latest-sws-survey","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/afp.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received a high public satisfaction rating for its performance, with an \"excellent +76\" net score, according to the recent December 2022 Social Weather Stations (SWS) Survey.<br /><br />This raised the net satisfaction of the AFP by nine (9) points from the net of +67 in December 2021.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/afp.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-24T10:57:33+08:00","hits":442},{"id":970,"title":"CSAFP dons rank to newly-promoted senior AFP officers","slug":"csafp-dons-rank-to-newly-promoted-senior-afp-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—</strong>The Chief of Staff AFP (CSAFP) General Andres C Centino, presided over the donning of ranks to nine senior AFP officers on January 19 and 20 at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo and at Headquarters Western Mindanao Command in Zamboanga City.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Promoted to the rank of Major General were BGen Edgar M Cardinoza PAF, commander of the AFP Health Service Command; BGen Jose Maria R Cuerpo II PA, the Deputy Chief of Staff for Personnel, J1; BGen Leonel M Nicolas PA, the Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence, J2; and BGen Marvin L Licudine PA, commander of the AFP Education, Training, and Doctrine Command.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-20T10:50:03+08:00","hits":780},{"id":971,"title":"MGen Galido assumes as new WESMINCOM commander","slug":"mgen-galido-assumes-as-new-wesmincom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/IMG-8425.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"479\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP installed MGen Roy M Galido PA as the new commander of the Western Mindanao Command (WESMINCOM) in a change of command ceremony on Friday, January 20, presided by the CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, at the WESMINCOM headquarters in Zamboanga City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/IMG-8425.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-20T10:18:38+08:00","hits":375},{"id":972,"title":"AFP employs PAF assets for HADR","slug":"afp-employs-paf-assets-for-hadr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/DR1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Armed Forces of the Philippines employs the Philippine Air Force’s C-295 aircrafts to transport 500 boxes of relief goods to Tandag, Surigao Del Sur and 100 wheelchairs to Roxas City, Capiz on January 17.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A C-295 medium-lift aircraft of the 220th Airlift Wing transported 500 boxes of relief goods from the Office of the Vice President to Tandag, Surigao Del Sur for those who were affected by severe flooding.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/DR1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-18T10:15:02+08:00","hits":14675},{"id":973,"title":"AFP dons 3-star ranks to top military officers","slug":"afp-dons-3-star-ranks-to-top-military-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/donning.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"494\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines dons three- star ranks to the newly promoted military officers at the ceremony presided over by the CSAFP, General Andres C Centino PA, on Thursday, January 12, here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Promoted to the rank of Lieutenant General were MGen Arthur M Cordura PAF, the Vice Chief of Staff AFP, and MGen Efren P Baluyot PA, the Commander of the Southern Luzon Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/donning.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-12T10:05:48+08:00","hits":358},{"id":974,"title":"CHANGE OF CHIEF OF OFFICE","slug":"change-of-chief-of-office","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/CC1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP welcomed its new Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training, and Doctrine, J8, in a Change of Chief of Office Ceremony presided over by The Deputy Chief of Staff VAdm Rommel Anthony Reyes on Thursday, January 12, in Camp Aguinaldo. BGen Fernando Reyeg, the Assistant J8, assumed the post in an acting capacity, replacing RAdm Donn Anthony Miraflor who was designated as the commander of the Naval Forces Western Mindanao.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-12T10:02:46+08:00","hits":955},{"id":975,"title":"DND-AFP holds the traditional New Year’s Call","slug":"dnd-afp-holds-the-traditional-new-year-s-call","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p> </p>\r\n<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/NY9.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"535\" />CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held the traditional New Year’s Call with AFP Chief of Staff General Andres Centino at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country on Wednesday, January 11.<br /><br />The AFP New Year’s Call was held jointly with the Department of National Defense. Military commanders from the Army, Air Force and Navy as well as chiefs of offices, senior staff officers, and senior enlisted personnel, together with their spouses attended the event. Also present were defense attachés and officials from the General Headquarters civilian human resources department.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/NY9.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-11T09:57:55+08:00","hits":367},{"id":976,"title":"CSAFP meets with the Turkish Ambassador","slug":"csafp-meets-with-the-turkish-ambassador","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/TUR3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"609\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres C Centino met with the Ambassador of Turkey, Niyazi Eyren Akyol during the latter's courtesy call on January 10 at the General Headquarters.<br /><br />In their meeting, the CSAFP expressed his gratitude for the significant contribution of the Government of Turkey to the AFP modernization with the acquisition of the Philippine Air Force Attack Helicopter (AHAP T129) and Philippine Army M113 APC Fire Power Upgrade.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/TUR3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-10T09:52:26+08:00","hits":218},{"id":977,"title":"AFP Statement on Change of Command","slug":"afp-statement-on-change-of-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Change of Command of the Chief of Staff, AFP went on smoothly this morning between the outgoing, LT GEN BARTOLOME VICENTE O BACARRO PA, to the incoming, GEN ANDRES C CENTINO PA. As a professional organization, the whole AFP is united behind the leadership of GEN CENTINO as it continues to perform its mission of protecting the people and defending territorial integrity and national sovereignty.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-09T09:45:17+08:00","hits":233},{"id":978,"title":" On the assumption of General Andres Centino as the 59th AFP Chief of Staff","slug":"on-the-assumption-of-general-andres-centino-as-the-59th-afp-chief-of-staff","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomes the designation of General Andres Centino PA as Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As a professional organization, the AFP supports the decision of the Commander-in-Chief, His Excellency Ferdinand R Marcos Jr. The AFP will continue in its mission to defeat all armed threat groups for the security and safety of our people, for the defense of our territorial integrity and national sovereignty.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-09T09:41:49+08:00","hits":219},{"id":979,"title":"AFP welcomes General Centino as 59th Chief of Staff, bids farewell to Lieutenant General Bacarro","slug":"afp-welcomes-general-centino-as-59th-chief-of-staff-bids-farewell-to-lieutenant-general-bacarro","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/AFP welcomes General Centino as 59th Chief of Staff bids farewell to Lieutenant General Bacarro.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"529\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> - The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomed General Andres C Centino as its 59th Chief of Staff, replacing Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro in a change of command ceremony held on Saturday, January 7.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The ceremony was presided over by Executive Secretary Lucas Bersamin at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo. General Centino took his oath before President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. in Malacañan Palace on January 6 following his appointment to hold the top military position.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/AFP%20welcomes%20General%20Centino%20as%2059th%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20bids%20farewell%20to%20Lieutenant%20General%20Bacarro.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-07T09:31:37+08:00","hits":288},{"id":980,"title":"AFP transports, secures 5th Philippine visit of St. Therese relics","slug":"afp-transports-secures-5th-philippine-visit-of-st-therese-relics","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/323782351_722651929291658_3660981028670152768_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"531\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) is providing land, sea and air transportation support as well as manpower to ensure the safe and successful tour of the relics of St. Therese of the Child Jesus across the country.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The relic of the Little Flower of Jesus arrived in Pasay City from Lisieux, France on Monday, January 2 which coincided with her 150th birth anniversary. It also marked the 5th Philippine visit of the pilgrim relic which will make the rounds of various dioceses and selected military chaplaincies until April 30.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/323782351_722651929291658_3660981028670152768_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-06T00:47:07+08:00","hits":237},{"id":981,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff joins PBBM Send-Off Ceremony ","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-joins-pbbm-send-off-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/viber_image_2023-01-03_17-26-37-157.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>SEND-OFF CEREMONY</strong> | The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro joined the send-off ceremony for President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr at the Villamor Air Base, Pasay City on Tuesday, January 3.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/viber_image_2023-01-03_17-26-37-157.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-04T08:33:53+08:00","hits":252},{"id":982,"title":"AFP Statement on the Appointment of Secretary Galvez","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-appointment-of-secretary-galvez-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan 2023/press.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\r\n<p>The AFP welcomes the appointment of Secretary Carlito Galvez Jr as the new Secretary of National Defense.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Jan%202023/press.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-01-01T01:48:16+08:00","hits":241},{"id":983,"title":"AFP joins 126th Rizal Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-126th-rizal-day-commemoration","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -</strong> The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) led by its Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro participated in the commemoration of the 126th anniversary of the martyrdom of Dr. Jose P. Rizal on Friday, December 30 at the Rizal National Monument in Manila.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">This year’s celebration was anchored on the theme “Rizal: Alaalang Iningatan, Yaman Ngayon ng Bayan''. It was highlighted by the traditional flag raising and wreath laying ceremonies in Rizal Park led by President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr as guest of honor and speaker.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-30T10:10:43+08:00","hits":216},{"id":984,"title":"Strategic losses mark communist group’s anniversary","slug":"strategic-losses-mark-communist-group-s-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march 2023/IMG-ea4363e5deda7f013d9fd24d384226a8-V.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/march 2023/IMG-ea4363e5deda7f013d9fd24d384226a8-V.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The communist terrorist group suffered significant strategic losses ahead of its anniversary on December 26, as it lost a great number of its guerilla units, leaders, and members.</p>\r\n<p><br />In 2022, the CTG was reduced to 2,112 members with 1,876 firearms as a result of the AFP’s campaign and the whole-of-nation program being implemented by the NTF-ELCAC. Likewise, their guerilla fronts were reduced to 22 from 89 six years ago. Seventeen of these were already classified as weakened while the remaining five (5) guerilla fronts are now the focus of relentless focused military operations and synergized efforts employing the whole-of-nation approach.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/march%202023/IMG-ea4363e5deda7f013d9fd24d384226a8-V.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-26T02:13:41+08:00","hits":274},{"id":985,"title":"ROTC GAMES 2023","slug":"rotc-games-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente<img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/8C68FCAC-49BC-4036-80EF-418F97062FC8.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/8C68FCAC-49BC-4036-80EF-418F97062FC8.jpeg\" /> Bacarro witnessed the signing of the pact establishing the ROTC Games during the joint signing and launching ceremony on Friday, December 23, at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/8C68FCAC-49BC-4036-80EF-418F97062FC8.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-23T10:22:40+08:00","hits":413},{"id":986,"title":"AFP fetes outstanding units, partners for role in peace-building","slug":"afp-fetes-outstanding-units-partners-for-role-in-peace-building","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/B73DB098-D59D-4252-A4A7-7360BC516214.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"536\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/B73DB098-D59D-4252-A4A7-7360BC516214.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) presented a Kapayapaan Award to its partners for their invaluable and continuing support to the military during the recognition ceremony as part of the 87th AFP anniversary on December 21.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Campaign Streamer awards were also given to military units that were instrumental in the dismantling of the communist terrorist group’s (CTG) guerilla fronts and vertical units contributing to the AFP's strategic victory against the CTG.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/B73DB098-D59D-4252-A4A7-7360BC516214.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-21T10:26:27+08:00","hits":250},{"id":987,"title":"ARRIVAL HONORS","slug":"arrival-honors","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/AH3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/AH3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP led by the Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro rendered full military honors to President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. upon his arrival at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo for the 87th AFP anniversary rites on December 19.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/AH3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-20T10:37:13+08:00","hits":620},{"id":988,"title":"PBBM leads AFP’s 87th-anniversary rites","slug":"pbbm-leads-afp-s-87th-anniversary-rites","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The President and Commander in Chief His Excellency Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr leads the 87th founding anniversary rites of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Monday, December 19 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand here.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">With this year’s theme, “AFP@87: Kaisa ng Sambayanan Tungo sa Mapayapa, Matatag, at Maunlad na Pilipinas,” the celebration aimed to highlight the military’s accomplishments and contributions to the country’s peace and security in the past year.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">As part of the ceremony, the military highlighted some of its game-changing assets as part of its modernization program. Philippine Air Force's FA-50 jets fly above the Camp Aguinaldo ground in a high-speed opener for the pass-in review and parade of ground followed by fly-by contingents.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/AN1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-20T10:33:46+08:00","hits":3951},{"id":989,"title":"AWARDING CEREMONY","slug":"awarding-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/AW20.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/AW20.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr leads the awarding ceremony during the AFP’s 87th Anniversary Rites at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. Six military personnel and two civilian human resources were recognized for their services and contributions to the accomplishment of the AFP mission.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/AW20.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-20T10:29:44+08:00","hits":344},{"id":990,"title":"AFP pays tribute to fallen soldiers","slug":"afp-pays-tribute-to-fallen-soldiers-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/viber_image_2022-12-16_15-51-53-057.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/viber_image_2022-12-16_15-51-53-057.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a wreath-laying ceremony to honor the soldiers who made the ultimate sacrifice in the line of duty on Friday, December 16, at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier at the Libingan ng Mga Bayani in Taguig City and at major AFP camps nationwide.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, AFP Chief of Staff, led the ceremony in Libingan ng Mga Bayani as part of the activities in line with the 87th AFP Anniversary on December 21.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/viber_image_2022-12-16_15-51-53-057.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-16T10:51:58+08:00","hits":308},{"id":991,"title":"54 AFP senior officers get CA nod","slug":"54-afp-senior-officers-get-ca-nod","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/CA6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"438\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/CA6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Fifty-four senior officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received confirmation on their ad-interim appointments from the Commission on Appointments (CA) on Wednesday, December 14, at the Senate Hall, in Pasay City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">PMA Superintendent, LtGen Rowen Tolentino, led the contingent of AFP officers. Rep. Jurdin Jesus Romualdo, the chairperson of the Committee on National Defense, recommended the confirmation which was then approved by the committee without objections.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/CA6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-15T11:08:06+08:00","hits":186},{"id":992,"title":"AFP to celebrate its 87th Founding Anniversary","slug":"afp-to-celebrate-its-87th-founding-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) will hold an anniversary program to celebrate its 87th anniversary on December 19 at Lapu-Lapu Grandstand, Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. With the theme, \"AFP @87: Kaisa ng Buong Sabayanan Tungo sa Mapayapa, Matatag at Maunlad na Pilipinas,\" the AFP aims to showcase our transformation and advancement as a military organization through the display of these assets.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-15T11:06:09+08:00","hits":575},{"id":993,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff honors fallen heroes at 5ID","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-honors-fallen-heroes-at-5id","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/5ID5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/5ID5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Camp Aguinaldo, QUEZON CITY – AFP Chief of Staff, LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro honors our fallen heroes through a wreath-laying ceremony rendered during his visit to Headquarters 5th Infantry Division (5ID), Camp Melchor F Dela Cruz, Upi, Gamu, Isabela on Dec 12.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LtGen Bacarro paid tribute to the fallen heroes of 5ID who sacrificed to protect the people of Northern Luzon from the atrocities of the communist terrorist group.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/5ID5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-13T13:31:36+08:00","hits":290},{"id":994,"title":"CSAFP meets with the Norwegian Ambassador","slug":"csafp-meets-with-the-norwegian-ambassador","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/NOR6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/NOR6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/NOR6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/NOR6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP) LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, met with the Norwegian Ambassador to the Philippines, His Excellency Christian Halaas Lyster, during his introductory call on December 12 at General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In their meeting, Ambassador Lyster and the CSAFP discussed both countries' adherence to human rights and IHL in addressing external and internal security issues.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/NOR6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-13T11:11:11+08:00","hits":219},{"id":995,"title":"AFP, UNODC sign Declaration of Cooperation on common interests","slug":"afp-unodc-sign-declaration-of-cooperation-on-common-interests","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/SI3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/SI3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City— The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the UN Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) signed a Declaration of Cooperation on December 12 at the General Headquarters here, setting a start of a partnership between the two institutions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff, LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro signed the declaration for the AFP, with Mr. Oliver Georges-Lermet, Senior Policy Advisor and Head of UNODC in the Philippines.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/SI3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-12T13:33:59+08:00","hits":186},{"id":996,"title":"Chief of Staff, AFP leads demilitarization of firearms in Maguindanao","slug":"chief-of-staff-afp-leads-demilitarization-of-firearms-in-maguindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/E6855127-4C57-469F-993D-FFBCC594720D.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/E6855127-4C57-469F-993D-FFBCC594720D.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro (CSAFP) spearheaded the demilitarization of the 307 captured, confiscated, surrendered, and recovered (CCSR) firearms and equipment at Headquarters 6ID in Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao on December 9.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The activity is one of the highlights during the CSAFP's visit to 6ID headquarters in time for the celebration of the yuletide season. It aims to boost the morale of the troops, especially those who will still be on duty during the yuletide break.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/E6855127-4C57-469F-993D-FFBCC594720D.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-11T13:36:48+08:00","hits":410},{"id":997,"title":"Army's Multi-capable Force celebrates 4th anniversary","slug":"armys-multi-capable-force-celebrates-4th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/E963FC13-7EC2-49DC-B89B-9474E8A041C9.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/E963FC13-7EC2-49DC-B89B-9474E8A041C9.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Philippine Army's First Brigade Combat Team (1BCT) celebrated its fourth founding anniversary on Friday, December 9, at its headquarters in Sultan Kudarat, Maguindanao Del Norte with the AFP Chief of Staff, LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro as the guest of honor and speaker.</p>\r\n<p>The 1BCT is the Army’s contingency force that is capable of addressing conventional, unconventional, and asymmetric threats. Activated in 2018, its first deployment was in Sulu to ensure peace and security in the region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/E963FC13-7EC2-49DC-B89B-9474E8A041C9.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-10T13:44:35+08:00","hits":201},{"id":998,"title":"Wounded soldiers receive early christmas gift from the AFP","slug":"wounded-soldiers-receive-early-christmas-gift-from-the-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/90F0404F-7AD0-4326-837A-1FED17615B6D.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/90F0404F-7AD0-4326-837A-1FED17615B6D.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - In recognition of their heroism and sacrifices, battle casualties recovering at the V. Luna Medical Center (VLMC) received early Christmas gift from the Armed Forces of the Philippines on Wednesday, December 7, in time for the holiday season.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff, LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro led the distribution of gift packs to soldiers to boost their morale and let them feel the essence of the holiday season.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/90F0404F-7AD0-4326-837A-1FED17615B6D.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-10T13:42:58+08:00","hits":287},{"id":999,"title":"AFP hosts anniversary Fun-run","slug":"afp-hosts-anniversary-fun-run","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/63DD597F-1FA1-4346-9192-D134042628B7.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/63DD597F-1FA1-4346-9192-D134042628B7.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) hosted the first uniformed service fun-run since the COVID-19 pandemic as part of its pre-87th AFP Anniversary activities at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on Friday, December 9.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Over 500 runners composed of uniformed and non-uniformed personnel from the General Headquarters, Army, Navy, Air Force, Philippine National Police, Bureau of Jail Management and Penology, and Bureau of Fire Protection participated in the activity in either five or ten kilometers categories.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/63DD597F-1FA1-4346-9192-D134042628B7.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-10T13:41:15+08:00","hits":461},{"id":1000,"title":"Youths paid tribute to soldiers in AFP anniversary concert","slug":"youths-paid-tribute-to-soldiers-in-afp-anniversary-concert","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/93EF2C53-572D-4887-A38E-A472AB3F3051.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"426\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/93EF2C53-572D-4887-A38E-A472AB3F3051.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Various bands from different youth organizations nationwide offered a tribute to members of the Armed Forces of the Philippines in a concert held at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand, in Camp Aguinaldo on December 9, as part of the military’s 87th-anniversary activities.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The activity dubbed Talented, Responsible, Innovative and Brave (TRIB) - Youth to the Peacemakers is a concert and cultural presentation of various youth groups and AFP bands that aims to honor the sacrifices of the soldiers in performing their duties in protecting the people and securing the state.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/93EF2C53-572D-4887-A38E-A472AB3F3051.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-10T13:39:04+08:00","hits":242},{"id":1001,"title":"REGIONAL SECURITY COOPERATION","slug":"regional-security-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/VIE1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/VIE1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro welcomes H.E. Mr. HOANG HUY CHUNG, Vietnamese Ambassador to the Philippines during the latter's courtesy call at the General Headquarters on Wednesday, December 7.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ambassador Hoang and CSAFP discussed security and stability and the need for an enhanced dialogue and cooperation to effectively address challenges in the region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/VIE1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-09T13:49:15+08:00","hits":216},{"id":1002,"title":"AFP reaffirms protection, promotion of Human Rights","slug":"afp-reaffirms-protection-promotion-of-human-rights","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/CC3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/CC3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City— In celebration of this year's National Human Rights Consciousness Week, members of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) pledged to continue the protection and promotion of Human Rights during the flag-raising ceremony held on Monday, December 5, at the AFP General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP Major General Arthur Cordura who represented the AFP Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, presided over the ceremony, which was attended by Officers, Enlisted Personnel, and Civilian Human Resources of the AFP.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/CC3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-06T13:52:10+08:00","hits":193},{"id":1003,"title":"AFP commits support on putting an end to HIV/AIDS","slug":"afp-commits-support-on-putting-an-end-to-hiv-aids","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/HIV3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"572\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/HIV3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City – The AFP affirms its commitment to support in putting an end to HIV/AIDS as it joins the World AIDS Day 2022 held at the Tejeros Hall, AFPCOC, Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on December 2, 2022, with the theme: “Unifying the Armed Forces Towards Ending HIV/AIDS Amidst the Challenges and Pandemics”.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">World AIDS day is observed every December 1 to bring awareness and encourage HIV/AIDS prevention, treatment, and care.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/HIV3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-05T14:08:40+08:00","hits":374},{"id":1004,"title":"ROTC cadets gather in 2022’s ROTC Summit","slug":"rotc-cadets-gather-in-2022-s-rotc-summit","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/ROTC5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/ROTC5.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Cadets and officers of ROTC programs nationwide gathered in this year’s ROTC summit held at the Tejeros Hall here and online on December 3 with AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro as the Guest of Honor and Speaker.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">With the theme, “ROTC Cadets of Today, Leaders of Tomorrow,” the Summit aims to advocate the promotion of the ROTC and highlight the enhancement of the reserve force of the AFP.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/ROTC5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-05T13:57:04+08:00","hits":349},{"id":1005,"title":"AFP switches on Christmas lights at military camps","slug":"afp-switches-on-christmas-lights-at-military-camps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December 2022/XMAS1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"451\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/December 2022/XMAS1.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City - Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro led the Thanks-giving mass and Christmas tree lighting ceremony at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand, Camp Aguinaldo on Friday, December 2.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The military camps nationwide simultaneously lit up their Christmas trees on Friday, an event meant to inspire joy and hope, and awaken the spirit of nationalism and love of service in all soldiers.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/December%202022/XMAS1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-12-05T13:54:52+08:00","hits":230}]}